msgid ":meth:`~.Item.set_motion_blur` :meth:`~.Item.is_motion_blur_enabled`"
msgstr ":meth:`~.Item.set_motion_blur` :meth:`~.Item.is_motion_blur_enabled`"

#: ../../source/tutorials/motion_blur.rst:23
msgid "其中两个方块的运动完全相同，唯一的区别是上方方块调用了 ``set_motion_blur()``："
msgstr ""
"Both squares perform exactly the same motion; the only difference is that "
"the upper one calls ``set_motion_blur()``:"

#: ../../source/tutorials/motion_blur.rst:25
msgid "开模糊的方块在每个时间样本中的位置都不同，采样再平均后就成了一条拖影；"
msgstr ""
"The blurred square occupies a different position in every time sample, so "
"averaging them turns it into a single trail;"

#: ../../source/tutorials/motion_blur.rst:26
msgid "未开启的方块则被固定在帧中心时刻，因此始终清晰锐利。"
msgstr ""
"the square that does not enable it is pinned to the frame's center time, so "
"it stays perfectly sharp."

#: ../../source/tutorials/motion_blur.rst:28
msgid "``set_motion_blur(False)`` 可以关闭；默认同时作用于后代，传入 ``root_only=True`` 则只修改物件自身。"
msgstr ""
"``set_motion_blur(False)`` turns it off; by default descendants are affected "
"as well, while ``root_only=True`` only changes the item itself."

#: ../../source/tutorials/motion_blur.rst:31
msgid "快门采样机制"
msgstr "How Shutter Sampling Works"

#: ../../source/tutorials/motion_blur.rst:33
msgid "每帧的曝光区间以该帧时间 ``t`` 为中心对称分布，区间的宽度由 ``motion_blur_shutter`` 决定："
msgstr ""
"The exposure interval of each frame is symmetric about that frame's time "
"``t``, and its width is decided by ``motion_blur_shutter``:"

#: ../../source/tutorials/motion_blur.rst:35
msgid ""
"曝光区间 = [t - motion_blur_shutter / fps / 2, t + motion_blur_shutter / fps "
"/ 2]"
msgstr ""
"exposure interval = [t - motion_blur_shutter / fps / 2, t + "
"motion_blur_shutter / fps / 2]"

#: ../../source/tutorials/motion_blur.rst:39
msgid ""
"``motion_blur_shutter`` 的单位是 ``1 / fps``（一帧时长），而不是秒。 例如 "
"``fps=30``、``motion_blur_shutter=6`` 表示每帧曝光 0.2 秒。"
msgstr ""
"``motion_blur_shutter`` is measured in units of ``1 / fps`` (one frame "
"duration), not seconds. For example, ``fps=30`` with "
"``motion_blur_shutter=6`` means each frame is exposed for 0.2 seconds."

